# Project core

## Layout

- **`app/`** — Next.js App Router: `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, UI under `app/ui/`, data loading under `app/services/` (e.g. YAML/resume loaders).
- **`tests/`** — Vitest + Testing Library; files match `tests/**/*.test.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}` (see `vitest.config.ts`).
- **`scripts/`** — Build/support scripts (ESLint ignores this tree).

## Path alias

- `@/*` maps to the repository root (`tsconfig.json` `paths`). Prefer `@/app/...` and `@/tests/...` for imports.

## Commands

- `npm run dev` — Next dev server
- `npm run build` — production build
- `npm run test` — Vitest (watch)
- `npm run lint` — ESLint
- `npm run format` — Prettier write

## Editing discipline

- Keep changes minimal and scoped to the task; avoid unrelated refactors.
- Match naming, import style, and quote style used in neighboring files in the same directory.
- Formatting: Prettier is the source of truth for formatting; ESLint handles lint rules (see `eslint.config.mjs`). Do not fight Prettier with manual layout.

## Scope

- Restrict edits to this repository/worktree unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.
